    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/solution-architect-identity-and-access-management-idam-in-parramatta-au-jid-484": {
      "title": "Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM)",
      "description": "Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Division Operations __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1657E Apply Shortlist Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9. Parramatta South Campus $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Shape the future of identity security across a complex, connected enterprise. Identity is at the heart of modern cyber security. From Zero Trust and privileged access to identity governance and cloud connectivity, the architecture decisions made today shape how securely and seamlessly people access the systems and services they rely on. At Western Sydney University, we're looking for a Senior Solution Architect, Identity & Access Management (IDAM) to bring technical depth, architectural leadership and a forward-thinking approach to our evolving digital environment. This is an opportunity to influence strategic technology initiatives across a large, complex organisation, designing secure, scalable and sustainable identity solutions that make a real difference. The Opportunity You'll lead solution architecture across a portfolio of strategic programs and projects, with a primary focus on Identity and Access Management and a secondary focus on Azure infrastructure and networking. Working within our Enterprise Architecture practice and alongside the Portfolio Management Office, you'll turn complex business and technology needs into clear architectural direction, practical designs and implementation roadmaps. Your focus will be the University's identity ecosystem, spanning Microsoft Entra ID, Okta SSO/MFA, Saviynt Identity Governance and Administration (IGA), CyberArk Privileged Access Management (PAM), identity provisioning and lifecycle management, authentication, authorisation, federation and Zero Trust architecture. You'll assess emerging requirements, challenge design assumptions and evaluate architectural options to deliver solutions that balance security, usability, cost, delivery priorities and long-term sustainability. You'll have the opportunity to influence how identity capabilities evolve across the University, ensuring security is embedded by design rather than added as an afterthought. You'll also bring architectural guidance across Azure infrastructure and networking, including landing zones, hybrid and private connectivity, network segmentation, infrastructure security and cloud platform governance. Working in partnership with Enterprise, Cloud, Security, Integration, Data and Solution Architects, you'll connect identity, cloud and infrastructure design to deliver cohesive enterprise-wide outcomes. This role is ideal for an architect who enjoys solving complex problems, influencing technology direction and working collaboratively with delivery teams to turn architecture into outcomes. You'll help shape reusable patterns, strengthen architectural capability and guide strategic initiatives from design through to delivery. What Success Looks Like: Shape secure, scalable target-state architectures and implementation roadmaps that translate enterprise strategy into practical technology outcomes. Lead architectural design across key identity platforms and capabilities, including Microsoft Entra ID, Okta, Saviynt and CyberArk. Embed Zero Trust and secure-by-design principles into identity, access and supporting cloud architecture. Turn complex technical and business requirements into clear design options and evidence-based recommendations, balancing security, risk, cost and delivery needs. Influence stakeholders, architects, delivery teams and technology partners to achieve aligned, sustainable architectural outcomes. Provide clear architectural direction throughout project delivery, proactively managing design decisions, risks, dependencies and trade-offs. Strengthen the University's architecture practice through reusable standards, reference architectures, design patterns and knowledge sharing. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You You're an experienced architect who can move confidently between deep technical conversations and strategic decision-making. You understand how identity, security and cloud capabilities fit together, and can turn complex requirements into architecture that is secure, practical and built to last. Postgraduate qualifications in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems or a related discipline, or equivalent extensive experience. Demonstrated experience as a Senior Solution Architect, Identity Architect, Security Architect, Cloud Architect or in a comparable role within a complex enterprise environment. Strong hands-on architectural expertise across Identity and Access Management, including authentication, authorisation, federation, identity provisioning and lifecycle management, IGA and PAM. Experience developing target-state architectures, solution designs and implementation roadmaps, with the ability to connect technical decisions to broader enterprise strategy. Experience working within an Enterprise Architecture practice, applying architecture principles and governance while collaborating across technology domains. The ability to assess competing design options, communicate technical trade-offs and provide recommendations that balance security, business needs, risk and delivery outcomes. Strong stakeholder engagement, facilitation and communication skills, with the confidence to influence without direct authority. Experience using enterprise architecture repositories such as Orbus Infinity, LeanIX or equivalent. Experience with Microsoft Entra ID, Okta, Saviynt, CyberArk and Azure infrastructure and networking will be highly relevant. Enterprise Architecture, Solution Architecture or Security Architecture certifications, Microsoft Azure certifications, and experience in large or federated organisations will also be advantageous. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Balaji Rangaswami, Director, Enterprise Architect via b.rangaswami@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1657E . Closing Date: 11:59pm, Sunday 22 November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time unrestricted working rights in Australia at time of application, for the duration of the appointment. Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Typ