    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/learning-hub-senior-librarian-in-parramatta-au-jid-498": {
      "title": "Learning Hub Senior Librarian",
      "description": "Learning Hub Senior Librarian Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1659P Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Parramatta South Campus Salary: HEW Level 6 $97,693 – $104,713 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Lead student-centred Library Learning Hub services that strengthen academic, digital and information skills. The Opportunity We are seeking an experienced and organised Learning Hub Senior Librarian to join the Library Student Skills and Engagement team and help shape the delivery of high-quality, student-centred Learning Hub services across Western. In this role, you will take a lead role in coordinating Learning Hub services across Western’s campuses and online channels. You will oversee rostering, supervise and support Learning Hub Librarians, and provide training and guidance to staff and casuals to promote a consistent and engaging experience for students. Alongside your coordination responsibilities, you will remain connected to frontline service delivery, providing responsive support across face-to-face, online chat, phone and FAQ channels. You will assist students with a broad range of enquiries while helping them build the academic, digital and information skills they need to succeed at university. Working closely with the Learning Hub Coordinator and colleagues across the Library, you will help ensure services are accessible, inclusive and responsive to Western’s diverse student community, including undergraduate, postgraduate, regional and international students. You will use sound judgement and apply Library frameworks, service guidelines and University policies to support accurate, professional and student-focused outcomes. You will also help strengthen and evolve Learning Hub services by contributing to service evaluation, responding to feedback and identifying opportunities for continuous improvement. By staying current with library systems, digital tools and student support practices, you will help ensure the Learning Hub continues to provide relevant, welcoming and high-quality support wherever students engage with us. What Success Looks Like: Success in this role will see you combining strong coordination and people leadership with a genuine commitment to the student experience. You will: Coordinate rostering and resources to support effective Learning Hub services across campuses and online channels. Guide, support and develop Learning Hub Librarians and casual staff to deliver professional, accurate and student-centred services. Provide responsive enquiry and learning support across face-to-face and digital channels. Use feedback, service evaluation and emerging practices to identify and contribute to continuous improvement opportunities. Build strong working relationships across teams and campuses to create an inclusive, welcoming and respectful Library experience. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You You will be an experienced library or learning support professional who enjoys combining service coordination, team leadership and direct student engagement. Organised and approachable, you will bring sound judgement, strong communication skills and the confidence to coordinate services across a busy, multi-campus environment. You will bring: A degree in Library Studies or a relevant discipline, with eligibility for ALIA membership. Demonstrated experience delivering learning support services within an academic or library environment, including frontline services, digital and academic skills activities, and student engagement. Experience coordinating library services and providing leadership, supervision or guidance to staff, preferably within a senior or supervisory role. Strong knowledge of contemporary frontline library services, including online chat, phone and other digital service channels. Proven ability to plan, coordinate and roster services across physical and online environments. An understanding of academic skills development and the role libraries play in supporting student learning and success. Advanced digital literacy, with confidence using library management systems, digital tools and emerging technologies. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Linda Parker, Associate University Librarian Student Skills & Engagement via linda.parker@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1659P in your email. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Sunday 15th November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University's online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d