    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/managing-counsel-in-parramatta-au-jid-617": {
      "title": "Managing Counsel",
      "description": "Managing Counsel Division Vice-Chancellor & President __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF2030J Apply Shortlist Fulltime, 5-year fixed term contract, Senior-level position. Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Shape sound decisions through strategic, commercially focused legal advice. Provide strategic legal advice on complex commercial, research and governance matters across Western Sydney University. The Opportunity You will serve as a senior legal adviser within the Office of General Counsel and University Secretary, delivering strategic, commercial and practical advice across Western Sydney University. You will work independently under the broad direction of the General Counsel and University Secretary and act as second-in-command across the Legal function. You will lead the review, negotiation and drafting of complex research, commercial and information technology contracts. You will advise senior stakeholders on high-value transactions, corporate governance, regulatory compliance and legal risk, balancing commercial objectives with the University’s statutory obligations and risk appetite. You will support the development of University statutes, policies, systems and processes while identifying emerging legal and regulatory risks. You will also oversee external legal providers, strengthen relationships across the higher education sector, and coach and mentor legal team members to support their professional development. What Success Looks Like: Deliver authoritative, practical and commercially sound legal advice on matters of strategic importance. Negotiate and draft complex research, commercial and technology agreements that protect the University’s interests. Identify legal and regulatory risks early and implement effective governance, compliance and risk mitigation responses. Manage external legal providers to achieve timely, cost-effective and high-quality outcomes. Build the capability of the Legal function through effective leadership, coaching and professional development. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A law degree or equivalent qualification, with eligibility to practise law in New South Wales. An unrestricted NSW practising certificate, or the ability to obtain one before commencing. At least eight years’ post-admission experience as a senior lawyer, including research and commercial contracts and corporate governance. Extensive experience analysing complex contracts, legislation and regulatory instruments, supported by strong commercial acumen. Highly developed negotiation and communication skills, with the ability to explain complex legal matters to senior leaders and non-legal audiences. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Phillip Maloney, General Counsel and University Secretary via P.Maloney@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF2030J Closing Date: 11:59pm, Friday 20th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW 