    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/marketing-manager-product-and-domestic-in-richmond-au-jid-613": {
      "title": "Marketing Manager, Product and Domestic",
      "description": "Marketing Manager, Product and Domestic Division Western Sydney & External Engagement __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF2031G Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 9. Hawkesbury campus (with requirements to also travel to Parramatta and Campbelltown) with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead integrated domestic marketing strategies that position undergraduate and postgraduate programs for prospective students. . The Opportunity You will lead the development and delivery of integrated marketing strategies that support domestic student recruitment across Western Sydney University’s undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Your work will position the University’s programs competitively and connect prospective students with relevant study opportunities. You will provide strategic direction to embedded Marketing and Communications Business Partners, coordinating faculty-based recruitment plans with University-wide priorities. Working with faculty leaders, Future Students and central marketing teams, you will shape targeted campaigns and maintain a streamlined approach to market. You will oversee campaign briefs and partner with Content, Creative and Communications, Digital Operations, Website and Paid Media teams to deliver timely marketing activity. Using market research, competitive analysis and campaign performance data, you will recommend improvements, guide resource allocation and strengthen recruitment outcomes. What Success Looks Like: Deliver an integrated domestic recruitment strategy that connects faculty plans with University-wide priorities. Provide clear strategic direction to Marketing and Communications Business Partners. Lead coordinated domestic and faculty campaign delivery across creative, digital and paid media channels. Translate campaign performance, market research and competitor insights into practical recommendations. Maintain accurate, differentiated web content that meets brand, accessibility and quality standards. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A degree in marketing, communications, business or a related field, or extensive relevant senior management experience. Demonstrated experience developing and delivering audience acquisition marketing strategies. Proven ability to lead, mentor or oversee marketing professionals in a generalist marketing function. Strong strategic and analytical capability, with experience using data to guide marketing performance. High-level stakeholder management, communication, negotiation and relationship management skills. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Yasmin Spencer, Director, Marketing via Y.Spencer@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF2031G Closing Date: 11:59pm, Saturday 14th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: $64,589 –