    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/injury-management-coordinator-in-richmond-au-jid-609": {
      "title": "Injury Management Coordinator",
      "description": "Injury Management Coordinator Division Operations __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1934Q Apply Shortlist Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 level Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and build safe, sustainable return-to-work outcomes across Western. The Opportunity You will manage workers compensation claims, workplace rehabilitation and return-to-work programs across Western Sydney University and its entities. You will coordinate complex cases from injury reporting and claims administration through to investigation, treatment, suitable duties and sustainable return to work. You will work with staff, supervisors, People & Culture, insurers, health professionals and rehabilitation providers to develop practical return-to-work and reasonable adjustment arrangements. You will provide specialist advice on workers compensation, rehabilitation, injury management and legislative obligations, while maintaining clear policies, procedures, records and communications. Using claims, insurer, HRMS and finance data, you will identify emerging trends, monitor costs and performance, and prepare evidence-based reports and recommendations. You will also manage insurance renewal and financial administration, develop education and improvement initiatives, and support effective injury management governance and stakeholder engagement. What Success Looks Like: Manage complex workers compensation and rehabilitation cases through timely, proactive coordination. Deliver safe and sustainable return-to-work and reasonable adjustment outcomes. Provide authoritative advice and maintain effective policies, procedures and records. Turn claims, cost and performance data into practical recommendations and prevention initiatives. Strengthen supervisor capability through targeted education and stakeholder engagement. You will manage a caseload of 40+ open matters, including complex recovery plans. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A relevant postgraduate qualification or equivalent experience in health administration, allied health, rehabilitation coordination or a related field. Completed SIRA-approved Return to Work Coordinator training (or interstate equivalent). Minimum 3 years’ experience managing workers compensation claims, workplace rehabilitation cases. Extensive knowledge of injury management and workers compensation legislation, including relevant work health and safety and discrimination requirements. Strong analytical, communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills, including experience preparing reports, plans, procedures and assessments. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Paolo Spinetti, Director, Safety and Wellbeing via P.Spinetti@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1934Q Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 11th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: $64,589 – $68,763 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (full-time equival Reference 387b35f6-2988-4da0-8a15-532e5749ff43 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Learning Hub Senior Librarian Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Library (U75E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing positionBased at Western’s Parramatta South CampusSalary: HEW Level 6 $97,693 – $104,713 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Lead student-centred Library Learning Hub servi Reference f69cf2dc-2ab0-488f-a2dd-0dbd9f38be12 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Project Manager Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Strategy & Planning Brand Western Sydney University College Location Parramatta Business Unit Project Management (J17D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time ongoing positionRemuneration: $126,140 p.a. plus Superannuation and Leave LoadingBased at Parramatta City campus About The College Western Sydney University The College is a not-for-profit Reference a383e3b9-d4e3-45fe-81e6-333e4c7cc8df Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Managing Counsel Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Legal, Compliance & Governance (U47B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Senior Description Fulltime, 5-year fixed term contract, Senior-level position.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Shape sound decisions through strategic, commercially focused legal advice. Prov Reference 91f8de43-c1d2-4fcc-b29a-1a43450be13e Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer Indigenous Health (Indigenous Identified Rol