    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/head-of-indigenous-future-students-engagement-in-richmond-au-jid-608": {
      "title": "Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement",
      "description": "Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Division Western Sydney & External Engagement __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF2020A Apply Shortlist Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9. Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualification as authorised under Section 14(D) of the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act 1977. Applicants will be required to provide confirmation of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander identity in line with University requirements. Document and requirements are available here: Click here to view Confirmation of Identity for Indigenous Australian Staff The Opportunity You will lead the University’s Indigenous future student engagement and recruitment strategy, translating University strategy into an integrated approach to school engagement, pathways, community engagement and prospective student recruitment. Your leadership will strengthen aspiration, connection and participation among Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, families and communities, ensuring engagement is culturally responsive, relationship-led and focused on creating meaningful pathways to higher education. You will lead the prospective student journey from early engagement through to enrolment, providing strategic oversight of initiatives including Pathways to Dreaming, the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Entry Program, school and campus experiences, mentoring, information sessions and community engagement activities. You will lead a specialist portfolio and strengthen culturally responsive practice, partnerships and accountability. Drawing on program data, research, community insight and sector intelligence, you will evaluate impact, performance, strengthen participation and conversion outcomes, manage resources and risk, and provide informed strategic advice to senior University stakeholders. What Success Looks Like: Deliver an integrated Indigenous engagement and recruitment plan across schools, pathways, communities and prospective student programs. Strengthen pathways from early engagement to admission and enrolment through coordinated programs, scholarships and recruitment opportunities. Build trusted, sustained relationships with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students, families, Elders, schools and community organisations. Establish clear priorities, performance measures and reporting across the Indigenous prospective student pipeline. Use data and community insights to improve program performance, participation and culturally authentic student experiences. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You You are an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person and can meet the University’s confirmation of identity requirements. You hold a relevant tertiary qualification and have significant experience in Indigenous engagement, education, outreach, community engagement or student recruitment. You have demonstrated success leading Indigenous engagement, education, pathway or recruitment strategies that deliver measurable outcomes. You bring strong knowledge of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander education, communities and pathways into higher education. You can lead complex teams and programs, translate strategy into operational plans, and provide high-level advice to senior stakeholders. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Kellie Burke, Director, Domestic Student Recruitment via kellie.burke@westernsydney.edu.au Please include the job reference code REF2020A Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 11th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: $64,589 – $68,763 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (full-time equival Reference 387b35f6-2988-4da0-8a15-532e5749ff43 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Learning Hub Senior Librarian Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Library (U75E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing positionBased at Western’s Parramatta South CampusSalary: HEW Level 6 $97,693 – $104,713 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Lead student-centred Library Learning Hub servi Reference f69cf2dc-2ab0-488f-a2dd-0dbd9f38be12 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Project Manager Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Strategy & Planning Brand Western Sydney University College Location Parramatta Business Unit Project Management (J17D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time ongoing positionRemuneration: $126,140 p.a. plus Superannuation and Leave LoadingBased at Parramatta City campus About The College Western Sydney University The College is a not-for-profit Reference a383e3b9-d4e3-45fe-81e6-333e4c7cc8df Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Managing Counsel Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Legal, Compliance & Governance (U47B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Senior Description Fulltime, 5-year fixed term contract, Senior-level position.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Shape sound decisions through strategic, commercially focused legal advice. Prov Reference 91f8de43-c1d2-4fcc-b29a-1a43450be13e Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer Indigenous Health (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 1893440c-8d31-4505-8c31-77d403fe175f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Come and join our team at Hawkesbury campusSalary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into trusted i Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Surgery Salary Location Parkside Cres, Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Academic Description Part-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level C or D.Macarthur Clinical School location.Salary: Level C $152,333 – $174,978 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (Pro-rata). Level D $182,520 – Reference b61a3114-6e3c-4677-ae51-310555bda346 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
