    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/senior-technical-support-officer-anatomy-in-campbelltown-au-jid-563": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Support Officer, Anatomy",
      "description": "Senior Technical Support Officer, Anatomy Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Campbelltown, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1756N Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Campbelltown campus, with flexible working arrangements Salary: HEW Level 6 $99,159 – $106,284 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Current Hepatitis B Vaccination required Provide specialist anatomy technical support for safe, compliant teaching, research and management of cadaveric materials. The Opportunity Western Sydney University is seeking a Senior Technical Support Officer – Anatomy to provide specialist technical support for anatomy teaching and research within Teaching & Research Technical Services. The Senior Technical Support Officer will prepare practical teaching spaces, materials and equipment for anatomy and physiology classes, and provide technical instruction and safety guidance to staff and students during classes. The role will also support research activities through technical advice, training in the use of specialised equipment, procurement, data collection and coordination of equipment servicing. Additional responsibilities include maintaining Standard Operating Procedures, participating in audits and stocktakes, and contributing to continuous improvement initiatives across the Medical and Allied Health team. The position will support the safe, respectful and compliant operation of the University’s anatomy facilities and Body Donor Program. Responsibilities include anatomical embalming, dissection and prosection, preparation of high-quality teaching specimens, ongoing specimen maintenance and coordination of future specimen requirements. The role will maintain accurate records, conduct specimen audits and ensure human cadaveric materials are handled, stored and disposed of in accordance with relevant legislation, Australian Standards, and University requirements. The Senior Technical Support Officer will promote safe work practices across teaching and research facilities by completing risk assessments, conducting laboratory safety inductions and maintaining current safety documentation and chemical inventories. The role will oversee the safe receipt, handling, storage and disposal of chemical and biological materials, maintain Safety Data Sheets and chemical inventories, and implement corrective actions arising from safety and compliance audits. What Success Looks Like: Success in this position will be demonstrated through the delivery of safe, reliable and compliant technical services that enable high-quality anatomy teaching and research. This will be evident when: Anatomy teaching spaces, specimens, materials and equipment are accurately prepared and ready for scheduled practical classes. Cadaveric materials are skilfully dissected, embalmed and maintained, with all handling, recording, storage and disposal completed safely, respectfully and in accordance with legislative requirements. Anatomy facilities maintain accurate and complete records, meet operational and compliance requirements, and remain prepared for internal and external audits. Staff, students and researchers receive clear and practical technical instruction on specialised equipment, laboratory procedures and safe work practices. Standard Operating Procedures, risk assessments, chemical inventories and safety records remain current, accurate and consistently applied across teaching and research activities. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You The successful candidate will bring specialist anatomy expertise, sound technical judgement and a demonstrated commitment to safe, respectful and compliant practice. They will have: An undergraduate degree in Anatomy or Mortuary Science, or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training and experience. Extensive experience providing technical support for anatomy teaching and research, including preparing specialised facilities and working with human cadaveric materials. Demonstrated knowledge and expertise of human anatomy, cadaver dissection, prosection and embalming. Demonstrated knowledge and practical experience in embalming human cadaveric specimens, including solution preparation, identification, record keeping, storage and ongoing specimen maintenance. Sound working knowledge of the Anatomy Act 1977 (NSW) and other legislation, standards and procedures relevant to human cadaveric materials. Experience supporting laboratory safety, including risk assessments, safety inductions, chemical records, safe materials handling and responses to audit findings. Strong organisational and communication skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and work effectively within a multidisciplinary team. Special Requirements: Due to the nature of this role, successful candidates are required to be vaccinated against Hepatitis B, or be willing to obtain the vaccination prior to commencing employment. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Greg Fathers, Technical Manager, Health via G.Fathers@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1756N in your email. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Sunday 8th November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of the online application, candidates will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor 