    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/postdoctoral-research-fellow-in-restoring-resilient-groundcover-in-richmond-au-jid-603": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Restoring Resilient Groundcover",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Restoring Resilient Groundcover Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1974T Apply Shortlist Full-time, 3-Year Fixed-Term position at Academic Level A. Hawkesbury Campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $98,611 – $119,137 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Design field and glasshouse trials to restore drought-resilient groundcover across grassy woodlands and support partner uptake. The Opportunity In this role, you will contribute to the project ‘Drought Resilient Innovation – Seeding Economic and Ecological Diversity’, which aims to strengthen the diversity and functional resilience of native groundcover in grassy woodlands. You will design and deliver glasshouse and field-based trials that test restoration interventions, including site preparation, soil amendments, planting approaches and drought manipulations. Working with investigators and partner organisations, you will also support multi-site restoration trials across the NSW western slopes. You will analyse ecological data, monitor biodiversity outcomes and co-benefits, and communicate findings through scientific publications, technical reports, presentations and stakeholder-facing research products. You will translate evidence into practical restoration guidance and may contribute to the supervision and mentoring of Higher Degree Research students. What Success Looks Like: Deliver rigorous glasshouse and field trials that test current and novel restoration interventions. Implement multi-site restoration trials effectively with project collaborators. Analyse and interpret data for peer-reviewed publications, reports and presentations. Translate research findings into practical guidance for government, industry and land-management partners. Maintain rigorous research, data management, ethics and work health and safety practices. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A PhD, or progress towards formal completion of PhD thesis examination, in ecological restoration, soil ecology or a relevant field. Strong theoretical and practical knowledge of plant and soil ecology in grassy woodlands. Demonstrated experience designing, implementing and managing glasshouse or field-based restoration trials. Experience assessing aboveground and belowground restoration outcomes and undertaking climate-change manipulations. Strong communication and organisational skills, with the ability to publish research and deliver outcomes with multiple collaborators. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Professor Uffe Nielsen, Professor in Soil Invertebrate Ecology via U.Nielsen@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1974T. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Monday 23 November 2026. Working Rights: Employer Visa sponsorship will be provided if required. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: $64,589 – $68,763 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (full-time equival Reference 387b35f6-2988-4da0-8a15-532e5749ff43