    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/associate-professor-chronic-and-complex-care-in-parramatta-au-jid-602": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Chronic & Complex Care)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Chronic & Complex Care) Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1932W Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level D. Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $182,520 – $200,625 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead chronic and complex care research, nurse-led clinical trials and nursing education through health service partnerships. The Opportunity You will provide academic leadership in chronic and complex care, building the School’s research capacity and national profile. You will lead investigator-initiated, nurse-led clinical trials and pursue Category 1 research funding as Chief Investigator A. You will deepen collaborative partnerships with health services across the Western Sydney region, drawing on access to THRI and SPHERE to strengthen research translation and multi-site clinical research. You will foster interdisciplinary research teams and networks across the University, health services and the wider nursing profession. You will contribute to teaching and learning within the School’s new curriculum, including subject coordination in the Bachelor of Nursing. Through contemporary blended teaching, course and program development, supervision and mentoring, you will support educational quality across the School’s multi-campus workplace. What Success Looks Like: Build the School’s capacity to undertake chronic and complex care research. Lead funded, multi-site, nursing-led clinical trials and research teams. Secure Category 1 research funding as Chief Investigator A. Strengthen mature and productive partnerships with health services. Contribute to contemporary teaching, curriculum renewal and subject coordination. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A PhD in a relevant discipline and a strong record of research leadership. Current AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse, with Australian clinical experience. Teaching and research expertise in chronic and complex care. Experience leading funded, multi-site, nursing-led clinical trials. Demonstrated national leadership and experience advancing equity, diversity and inclusion in research and teaching. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Professor Caleb Ferguson, Dean, School of Nursing and Midwifery via C.Ferguson@westernsydney.edu.au. Please include the job reference code REF1932W. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Friday 6 November 2026. Checks: Appointment to this position is subject to a valid Working with Children Check (WWCC) for paid employment in accordance with the Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012 (NSW). Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: $64,589 – $68,763 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (full-time equival Reference 387b35f6-2988-4da0-8a15-532e5749ff43 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Learning Hub Senior Librar