    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/casual-student-success-coach-expressions-of-interest-in-parramatta-au-jid-599": {
      "title": "Casual Student Success Coach (Expressions of Interest)",
      "description": "Casual Student Success Coach (Expressions of Interest) Division Strategy & Planning __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Casual Job ID: REF1995O Apply Shortlist Casual Talent Pool $62.65 per hour | Casual Professional Employee Level 6 Casual opportunities available on an ad hoc basis across Bankstown City, Campbelltown, Kingswood, Liverpool City and Parramatta City campuses. Candidates are required to have wide availability, with hours varying according to operational requirements. NSW Employee Working with Children Check required. About The College Western Sydney University The College is a not-for-profit wholly owned entity of Western Sydney University. As you consider joining our dynamic team, know that you will be part of an organisation that values growth, inclusivity, and excellence. Learn more about The College here . About the Role The College is seeking highly motivated and adaptable individuals with strong interpersonal, coaching and mentoring skills to support students engaged in modular learning. As this is a casual opportunity, work will be offered on an ad hoc, relief basis to support operational needs across teaching periods. Working with the Student Success team, you will play an important role in supporting students to stay engaged, build confidence and succeed throughout their studies. As a Casual Student Success Coach, you will: Provide tailored one-on-one and group coaching that brings together pastoral care, academic support and career guidance. Support students to navigate challenges, recognise their achievements and remain engaged in their studies. Monitor student progress and contribute to strategies that support retention, engagement and overall student success. Contribute to the implementation of the Student Success Framework and initiatives that build belonging, inclusion and connection. Support students from diverse and underrepresented backgrounds, promoting equitable access to support and opportunities. Work collaboratively with academic and professional staff to resolve complex student matters, using sound judgement and solution-focused approaches. Advocate for student needs and contribute to the integration of coaching approaches into curriculum and teaching practices. Use technology and systems effectively to manage information, support students and deliver services across a dynamic environment. Eligibility To be eligible for casual employment, applicants must meet the below criteria: A relevant undergraduate qualification, or equivalent education and experience. Experience supporting student engagement, wellbeing or success in a tertiary setting, including the delivery of student-focused programs, workshops or resources. Understanding of coaching and mentoring approaches and their application in supporting student engagement and success. Experience working effectively with diverse and underrepresented student groups. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trust and rapport and provide clear, timely support in both face-to-face and online environments. Well-developed problem-solving skills and the ability to navigate complex or sensitive situations professionally. Ability to collaborate effectively with a range of academic and professional stakeholders across The College and University. Ability to work flexibly and adapt to changing priorities and operational needs. It is a mandatory requirement for all College employees to have a current NSW Employee Working with Children Check (WWCC) in accordance with the NSW Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012. About the Casual Community The Casual Community is open for eligible candidates to register an Expression of Interest (EoI) for casual employment with Western Sydney University, The College. The Casual Community enables The College to access suitable and experienced individuals for casual employment opportunities across a broad range of business areas at short notice, subject to the following: You will be engaged as and when required, and on an ad hoc and/or intermittent basis. The College does not guarantee the provision of ongoing or regular employment, and makes no firm advance commitment to continuing or indefinite work. Your application is not a guarantee that an offer of casual employment will be made. You will only be contacted regarding your application if an opportunity arises that matches your skills and experience. Applications remain active for 12 months Please Note: Previous applicants need not apply. Remuneration: Casual Professional Employee Level 6 – $62.65 per hour Enquiries: Please direct enquiries about this role to Shanna Robinson, Manager Student Engagement via email at S.Robinson@westernsydney.edu.au . Specific enquiries or issues with your application may be directed to the Talent Acquisition Team at talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . Closing date: 11:59pm, Tuesday 3 November 2026 Interviews: Please note interviews are expected to be held in the week commencing 9 November 2026. Expected commencement: January 2027 Working Rights in Australia - Eligibility This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. At the time of application, proof of your working rights in Australia must be provided. Please note, only those applications submitted via the WSU online recruitment system will be accepted. Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of 