    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/development-lawyer-in-parramatta-au-jid-577": {
      "title": "Development Lawyer",
      "description": "Development Lawyer Division Vice-Chancellor & President __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1921H Apply Shortlist Full-time, 5-year fixed term contract Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Competitive senior-level remuneration, commensurate with experience. Provide strategic legal advice on complex property, construction, environmental and planning matters across the University. The Opportunity In this role, you will take end-to-end ownership of a complex portfolio of property, construction, environmental and planning legal matters. Working within the Office of General Counsel, you will establish legal strategies, manage institutional risk and deliver commercially sound outcomes aligned with University objectives. You will provide authoritative advice to senior stakeholders and lead the structuring, drafting, negotiation and settlement of complex contracts, project documentation, agreements, disputes and memoranda of understanding. You will guide property transactions and major project opportunities, establishing appropriate legal, commercial and governance structures. You will advise on legislation, regulatory reviews, University policies and compliance initiatives, while managing external legal service providers for timely and cost-effective outcomes. You will also support the capability of the Office of General Counsel by mentoring junior lawyers and paralegals and sharing specialist knowledge. What Success Looks Like: Deliver commercially sound outcomes across complex property, construction, environmental and planning matters. Provide clear, authoritative legal advice that identifies risk and offers practical strategies. Lead the negotiation and settlement of complex legal documents and transactions. Establish effective legal, commercial and governance structures for major projects and property matters. Manage external legal service providers to achieve timely and cost-effective outcomes. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A law degree or equivalent qualification and registration, or eligibility for registration, to practise law in New South Wales. An unrestricted New South Wales practising certificate, or the ability to obtain one before commencement. At least seven years’ post-admission experience, including substantial property, construction, environmental and planning law experience. Demonstrated experience across property transactions, including acquisitions, disposals, leasing, licensing, easements and covenants. Strong commercial judgement, negotiation and communication skills, with the ability to advise senior and non-legal stakeholders. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Johan Haaring, Senior Development Lawyer via J.Haaring@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1921H Closing Date: 11:59pm, Tuesday 10th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Finance Business Partner Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Finance and Procurement (U76C) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Kingswood campus and travel required to other campuses with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Load Reference 1fd4719e-3a8e-4cb6-bf86-b69d542ebf33 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Solution Architect, Corporate Systems Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Fulltime, 12 month fixed term position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the architectu Reference 4fb91d2f-5c71-4f40-af40-c96bc9521647 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Solution Architect - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Chief Operating Officer (U76D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South Campus$139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape the future of identity security across a complex, co Reference eb843b48-d332-4186-a363-a35170a0b501 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Operations Assistant Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the Vice-Chancellor & President (U47A) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Professional Description 0.8 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 4.Parramatta South Campus with rostered start and finish times.Salary: